WEBVTT

00:22.601 --> 00:27.223
The monitors are humming in the artificial

00:27.343 --> 00:28.024
light

00:31.885 --> 00:34.727
I've been staring at the ceiling through a

00:34.787 --> 00:37.408
never-ending night

00:41.102 --> 00:46.205
I can't feel the floor beneath me, the gravity is

00:46.305 --> 00:47.245
gone

00:50.727 --> 00:55.709
Just a broken piece of metal, waiting for the

00:55.769 --> 00:56.470
dawn

01:00.158 --> 01:04.781
But I turn my heavy head and look across the room

01:05.182 --> 01:08.944
You're sleeping in the corner, a beacon in the

01:09.004 --> 01:13.027
gloom You didn't take the transport, you didn't

01:13.067 --> 01:17.510
fly away You planted down your boots and swore

01:17.551 --> 01:21.573
that you would stay The structural integrity's

01:21.613 --> 01:25.216
completely compromised But I can see the

01:25.336 --> 01:29.318
sanctuary reflecting in your eyes You cross the

01:29.438 --> 01:34.121
silent ward and you pull me to your chest Holding

01:34.161 --> 01:38.824
down the armor so the engine gets to rest You are

01:39.924 --> 01:45.027
the anchor's hold Keeping me from drifting out

01:45.227 --> 01:49.810
into the cold When the orbit was broken When the

01:49.850 --> 01:52.791
vessel was wrecked You wrapped your arms around

01:54.212 --> 01:59.534
The damage to protect A gravitational embrace

01:59.815 --> 02:04.457
In the middle of the dark Holding all the pieces

02:04.617 --> 02:08.599
Saving the spark I'm surviving the crash

02:08.719 --> 02:14.202
Because you wouldn't let me go You are the

02:14.522 --> 02:15.783
anchor's hope

02:24.325 --> 02:27.786
They're running the diagnostics, reading out

02:27.826 --> 02:33.508
the chart. They can fix the heavy machinery, but

02:33.588 --> 02:36.089
they cannot

02:37.329 --> 02:38.710
fix the heart. I

02:42.491 --> 02:46.512
was terrified of floating into the endless

02:46.592 --> 02:52.694
black, a ghost inside a machine that is never

02:55.591 --> 02:57.433
You're coming back

03:01.036 --> 03:04.259
But you're standing by the console, your hands

03:04.359 --> 03:09.043
upon the glass Refusing every order to let the

03:09.143 --> 03:14.047
moment pass You pull me in again, tighter than

03:14.107 --> 03:18.411
before We're fighting off the vacuum right here

03:18.551 --> 03:22.073
on the floor The structural integrity's

03:22.133 --> 03:25.695
completely compromised But I can see the

03:25.815 --> 03:29.737
sanctuary reflecting in your eyes You cross the

03:29.857 --> 03:34.499
silent ward and you pull me to your chest Holding

03:34.519 --> 03:37.601
down the armor so the engine gets to rest

03:40.782 --> 03:46.503
You are the anchors hold Keeping me from

03:46.563 --> 03:50.804
drifting out into the cold When the orbit was

03:50.904 --> 03:54.265
broken, when the vessel was wrecked You wrapped

03:54.325 --> 03:59.666
your arms around the damage to protect A

03:59.766 --> 04:04.167
gravitational embrace in the middle of the dark

04:04.667 --> 04:09.192
Holding all the pieces, saving the spark. I'm

04:09.252 --> 04:12.915
surviving the crash because you wouldn't let me

04:12.995 --> 04:18.020
go. You are the anchor's host.

04:32.848 --> 04:36.831
I can't

04:36.971 --> 04:46.657
feel my legs I can't feel the ground But I can feel

04:46.697 --> 04:57.123
your arms And I am safe and sound Are the anchors

04:57.204 --> 05:01.647
whole? Keeping me from drifting out into the

05:01.707 --> 05:06.051
cold When the orbit was broken, when the vessel

05:06.091 --> 05:09.874
was wrecked You wrapped your arms around the

05:09.994 --> 05:15.298
damage to protect A gravitational embrace in

05:15.318 --> 05:19.781
the middle of the dark Holding all the pieces,

05:19.901 --> 05:23.784
saving the spark I'm surviving the crash

05:23.864 --> 05:29.266
because you wouldn't let me go You are the

05:29.586 --> 05:34.388
anchor's hold Never

05:34.408 --> 05:40.090
let me go The gravitational embrace

05:42.831 --> 05:44.832
Holding me in place

